      "id": "wisconsin-holidays",
      "sourceUrl": "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/statutes/statutes/995/20",
      "title": "The legal holidays of Wisconsin (Wis. Stat. § 995.20) that\n`us-federal-holidays` does not already close: the days of the partisan\nprimary (the second Tuesday in August of an even year) and of the general\nelection in November (the Tuesday after the first Monday of November of an\neven year), from Wis. Stat. § 5.02, which is not vendored. The section's\nother days are federal holidays observed no later. Each `once` day is listed\nfrom the date of the vendored edition (in effect October 1, 2026) to the end\nof 2050. Not modeled: Good Friday, of which only 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. is\nobserved for worship, and the municipal-election holidays of a 1st class\ncity, which are local (a last day on one is the earlier date)."
    }
